    "ruling": "THE TILT IS THE FRAME'S, NOT WRIGHT'S. Two things say so and neither assumes anything about the drawing. First, every line of BOTH families tilts the same way; a rotation of the drawing under its registration tilts them equally and oppositely, so this is not one. Second, the section's four PLSS boundaries \u2014 lines that run true north and true east on the ground by definition \u2014 tilt in this frame by the same amount and the same way as the interior lines do. A frame that tilts a line known to be cardinal is telling you about itself. The mechanism is in `conformality`: the fit is a general affine with two different axis scales, so it does not preserve angles. The committed grid is rescaled onto the section's own statute-mile square, which takes that distortion out with the rest of it \u2014 so LEVEL IS RIGHT, and right for a stated reason rather than because a median was carried. The grade stays `inferred`: a tilt the frame puts on its own control is not attested by the survey."
